# Plan File Location

All plan files MUST live in the repository's `plans/` directory, never in `~/.cursor/plans/`.

## Rule

- Plans MUST be copied to: `<workspace_root>/plans/<plan_name>.plan.md`
- Keep the original at `~/.cursor/plans/` (Cursor's plan UI needs it)

## Why

- Plans should be version-controlled with the repository
- Team members can share and review plans
- Plans stay with the project they belong to

## Mandatory Procedure

The `CreatePlan` tool writes to `~/.cursor/plans/` by default and does not support custom paths. Therefore, IMMEDIATELY after every `CreatePlan` call:

1. Read the created file from `~/.cursor/plans/<filename>.plan.md`
2. Copy its contents to `<workspace_root>/plans/<filename>.plan.md`

Do NOT delete the file from `~/.cursor/plans/`. Keep both copies -- Cursor needs the original at `~/.cursor/plans/` for its plan UI, and the workspace copy ensures version control.

This is NOT optional. Every plan must be copied in the same turn it is created. Do not wait for the user to ask.
